# Firmware serial protocol

Firmware and host share one line contract — `<ms>,<TYPE>,<payload...>` — documented
in [firmware/PROTOCOL.md](../../firmware/PROTOCOL.md). Read it before changing
serial output, message types, commands, or framing.

- Any change to line format / message types / commands / framing → update
  [firmware/PROTOCOL.md](../../firmware/PROTOCOL.md) in the same change, and bump
  `PROTO_VERSION` when the contract itself changes.
- The host parses these lines through `host/protocol.py` (see docs/decisions/0024)
  — keep the two in sync so host tools don't break.
- Pin map and tunables live in `firmware/common/rig_config.h` (the host reads it
  too, see docs/decisions/0021) — not scattered magic constants.
